Press Start 2P, by CodeMan38, licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
Share Tech Mono, by Carrois Apostrophe, under the same licence. Both are loaded
from Google Fonts by web/index.html rather than shipped here.

adenosine, the browser engine whose AdRPG module provides the game loop and
input handling and whose score and chat clients the deployed page loads, is
Copyright 2026 magmacrunch media under the Apache License 2.0. It is a separate
repository and keeps that licence -- the engine is meant to be reused; this
game is not.

Note how little of it this game uses. AdRPG supplies a loop, a key-state map
and four booleans; every pixel is drawn by web/js/render.js and every rule
lives in web/js/stations.js. The music is deliberately not AdAudio's: that
module hardcodes looping and exposes neither an ended event nor a playback
position, and a round that *is* one play of a track needs all three.
